AuraDE installation and recovery environment

The boot menu has an entry for each way in, and picking one starts it for you:
the graphical installer, the text installer, or safe graphics for a machine
whose graphics stack does not cooperate. This console is the fourth entry, and
nothing was started on it.

Run `aurade-installer-start` to install AuraDE. It asks a few questions, shows
what it will do, and does not touch any disk until you confirm that disk by
name. It runs the graphical installer when this machine can display one and the
text installer when it cannot; both ask the same questions and run the same
engine.

Run `aurade-installer-start --safe-graphics` if the graphical installer never
draws anything, and `aurade-installer-tui` to go straight to the text
installer. Add NO_COLOR=1 for a plain-text session, or AURADE_FORCE_TUI=1 to
skip the graphics check.

Run `aurade-installer` for the older prompt-by-prompt flow.
Run `aurade-install --help` for noninteractive and image-based installs.
Run `aurade-recovery --help` for rollback and evidence collection.

WARNING: tty1 is a local installation console with an empty root password.
Do not expose this live session to an untrusted network or physical access.
Create a normal account password during installation; this live root account
is not copied to the installed system.
